<title>BELGIUM: Belgian producer prices up 0.96 pct in September.</title>
<headline>Belgian producer prices up 0.96 pct in September.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian Ministry of Economic Affairs released the following data -</p>
<p>    PRODUCER PRICES		 SEPT    AUG     JULY</p>
<p>    General index (base=1980)   139.29  137.97  137.66</p>
<p>    Change in pct vs pvs mth    +0.96   +0.23    n/a</p>
<p>    Food, drink, tobacco index  148.91  148.19  147.64</p>
<p>    Change in pct vs pvs mth    +0.49   +0.37    n/a</p>
<p>    Energy index		    103.84   99.18   98.35</p>
<p>    Change in pct vs pvs mth    +4.70   +0.84    n/a</p>
<p>    Index ex oil products	 148.06  147.72  147.54</p>
<p>    Change in pct vs pvs mth    +0.23   +0.12    n/a</p>
<p>NOTE - main increases were for the following products - petroleum, electricity, oils and fats, meat, milk and milk products and animals feeds;</p>
<p>	   - main decreases were for the following products - iron</p>
<p>and steel, non-ferrous metals, construction materials and paper and cardboard.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
